{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-223358","model_call":16,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ watermelon (+ expensive prices price) (+ due because caused) (+ drought weather rain harvest supply shortage))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ watermelon (+ expensive prices price) (+ due because caused) (+ drought weather rain harvest supply shortage))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_366358143#9_763370298","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2740","rank":1,"snippet":"Your Essay Find out how UKEssays.com can help you! Cite This Work DMCA / Removal Request \" , \"segment\": \"An example of scarcity and choice would be, watermelons, which are occasionally scarce due to the fact they grow in a limited time of year. When the supply of watermelon is limited, they become scarce. If watermelon becomes widely wanted when they are scarce, the demand for watermelons results in an increase. The demand increases because the product is limited, not <cover>because the price is low. As a result the consumer is faced with a choice, to decide if they are willing to pay a higher price for the scarce watermelon. Supply </cover>and demand are also affected by many other factors such as nature, government, income, populations, technology, seasonality, and price of materials and input, for example, during super bowl season the price of chicken wings increase significantly. Chicken farm producers increased prices on restaurants due to increased government regulations and increased cost of grain in winter. As a result, restaurants may purchase a lower quantity of chicken wings and increase their price to their customers. (“ Economic”, n.d). Find out how UKEssays.com can help you!"},"time":799},"model_calls":16,"document_judgments":11,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
