{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-223358","model_call":87,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ watermelon (+ shortage shortages scarce scarcity) (+ \"in season\" seasonal seasonality summer winter) (+ supply expensive prices))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ watermelon (+ shortage shortages scarce scarcity) (+ \"in season\" seasonal seasonality summer winter) (+ supply expensive prices))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_366358143#9_763370298","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2809","rank":1,"snippet":"\"An example of scarcity and choice would be, watermelons, which are occasionally scarce due to the fact they grow in a limited time of year. When the supply of watermelon is limited, they become scarce. If watermelon becomes widely wanted when they are scarce, the demand for watermelons results in an increase. The demand increases because the product is limited, not because the price is low. As a result the consumer is faced with a choice, to decide if they are willing to pay a higher price for the <cover>scarce watermelon. Supply and demand are also affected by many other factors such as nature, government, income, populations, technology, seasonality, </cover>and price of materials and input, for example, during super bowl season the price of chicken wings increase significantly. Chicken farm producers increased prices on restaurants due to increased government regulations and increased cost of grain in winter. As a result, restaurants may purchase a lower quantity of chicken wings and increase their price to their customers. (“ Economic”, n.d). Find out how UKEssays.com can help you!\" , \"start_char\": 4168.000000 , \"title\": \"How Scarcity and Choice Impact ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_366358143#9_763370298","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":508},"model_calls":87,"document_judgments":44,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-223358","model_call":87,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2809"},"model_calls":87,"document_judgments":44,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-223358","model_call":87,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2809"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2809"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_529377695#11_1211773180","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2809","rank":2,"snippet":"impact can’t be overstated. Our Newsletter \" , \"segment\": \"People were curious about Claws and boom: the following summer was a lawless smorgasbord of ever-so-slightly flavored booze-filled seltzers. Truly and other brands continued to try to compete, and did see success, but none will ever reach the level of notoriety of White Claw. Bros, basic bitches, wine moms, party dads, and college kids alike have all agreed: White Claw is the one. Everyone spent the <cover>summer of 2019 drinking it like it was going out of style, unknowingly threatening their supply. By September of that year, there was a shortage, which was a huge bummer, but didn’t last too long. Fast forward to March 2020, when the pandemic ended the party. But White Claw returned with even more flavors, including lemon, tangerine, and watermelon. </cover>Who knew booze would be what put seltzer on the map?\" , \"start_char\": 4740.000000 , \"title\": \"History of White Claw: How Did 'White Claw' Start? - Thrillist\" , \"url\": \"https://www.thrillist.com/news/nation/history-of-white-claw\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_366358143#9_763370298","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":10},"model_calls":87,"document_judgments":44,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
